-- A continuous mixture bound with `draw y = ...` whose condition reads a shared
-- continuous draw x, returned next to a comparison on that same x, is refused
-- in probability mode: "no inference engine applies to the binding of 'x'".
-- Inlining the single-use binding, `(x > 0.0, if x > 0.0 then Normal + 1.0 else
-- Normal)`, compiles and answers p((True, 1.5)) = 0.5 * N(1.5; 1, 1) =
-- 0.17603266338214976 (dim 1), so the refusal is a rewrite-invariance defect:
-- the same distribution, one spelling admitted, the other not. Idealized:
-- p((True, 1.5)) = (0.17603266338214976, dim 1); p((False, 0.0)) = 0.5 * N(0; 0, 1).
-- Found by experiments_nest systems-benchmarking-chapter (benchmark 3, model M3,
-- whose SPPL-equivalent compiles in SPPL). Verified on dev at compiler 8b8223d.
-- Ticket draw-bound-mixture-over-shared-continuous-condition-refused.
expect-failure: refused "no inference engine applies"
